---
description: Preserve existing SvelteKit hosts when running the Svartz CLI
globs:
  - packages/cli/**
  - packages/config/**
alwaysApply: false
---

# SvelteKit host ownership

- Detect an existing SvelteKit app at the Svartz config root before falling back to the repository's `apps/web` shell.
- A host app owns its routes, layouts, adapter, scripts, Vite config, and `.svelte-kit` directory. Build/dev inject `@svartz/vite` without rewriting host files. `init` may wrap the Vite default export once to keep virtual aliases in SvelteKit's secondary build; preserve the original config expression and existing scripts.
- `target: { type: "host" }` leaves adapter selection to the host. The CLI keeps repository-only adapter and Turbo behavior for the standalone `apps/web` shell.
- Svartz-generated artifacts stay under `.svartz/vaults/<id>`; the host's build output stays where its adapter puts it.
- Local workspace theme package builds use the package name, not a theme path. Ordinary host apps restart on local theme edits without running a pnpm workspace filter.
- A host build composes all configured host vaults in one Vite run. `virtual:svartz/host` selects mount-scoped artifact and theme modules; `virtual:svartz/artifacts` remains the single-vault contract. Keep generated asset output names under each mount to prevent filename collisions. `--vault` does not narrow a host build.
- Generated catchall pages import `virtual:svartz/tailwind-sources.css`; the host CSS entry includes Tailwind and scans packed theme/UI `dist`. `withSvartzHost` adds the Tailwind plugin only when the host has none. Custom catchalls keep ownership and must import the CSS entry themselves.
